// Define the maximum number of requests per second
const int MAX_REQUESTS_PER_SEC = 1000;

// Define the maximum number of concurrent threads
const int MAX_CONCURRENT_THREADS = 100;

// Define a struct to represent a device request
struct DeviceRequest {
    std::string deviceId;
    std::string networkProtocol;
    std::string data;
};

// Define a struct to represent the status of a device request
struct DeviceRequestStatus {
    int requestsProcessed;
    int requestsFailed;
    int requestsSuccessful;
};

// Define a map to store the status of all devices
std::map<std::string, DeviceRequestStatus> deviceStatusMap;

// Define a mutex to protect the deviceStatusMap
std::mutex deviceStatusMutex;

// Define a condition variable to signal when a request is processed
std::condition_variable requestProcessedCV;

// Define a function to handle a device request
void handleDeviceRequest(const DeviceRequest& request) {
    // Acquire the lock on the deviceStatusMap
    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(deviceStatusMutex);

    // Get the status of the device
    auto statusIt = deviceStatusMap.find(request.deviceId);
    if (statusIt == deviceStatusMap.end()) {
        // If the device is not found, create a new entry in the map
        DeviceRequestStatus status;
        status.requestsProcessed = 0;
        status.requestsFailed = 0;
        status.requestsSuccessful = 0;
        deviceStatusMap[request.deviceId] = status;
    }

    // Increment the number of requests processed for the device
    auto& status = deviceStatusMap[request.deviceId];
    status.requestsProcessed++;

    // Process the request
    try {
        // Send the request to the external API
        sendRequestToExternalAPI(request);

        // Increment the number of successful requests for the device
        status.requestsSuccessful++;
    } catch (const std::exception& e) {
        // If there is an error, increment the number of failed requests for the device
        status.requestsFailed++;
    }

    // Notify the main thread that a request has been processed
    requestProcessedCV.notify_all();
}

// Define a function to send a request to the external API
void sendRequestToExternalAPI(const DeviceRequest& request) {
    // Implement this function using the HTTP or HTTPS protocol, depending on the networkProtocol field of the request
}

// Define a function to handle the rate limits of the external API
bool checkRateLimit() {
    // Implement this function to check if the rate limit has been reached
}

// Define a function to automatically adjust the request rate based on current load and historical performance metrics
void adjustRequestRate() {
    // Implement this function to dynamically scale back the request rate during peak times without affecting overall service availability
}

// Define a main function to run the asynchronous data ingestion pipeline
int main() {
    // Initialize the deviceStatusMap and requestProcessedCV
    std::map<std::string, DeviceRequestStatus> deviceStatusMap;
    std::condition_variable requestProcessedCV;

    // Create a thread pool to handle concurrent requests
    std::vector<std::thread> threads;
    for (int i = 0; i < MAX_CONCURRENT_THREADS; i++) {
        threads.emplace_back(handleDeviceRequest);
    }

    // Continuously read device requests from the input stream
    std::ifstream in("input.txt");
    while (true) {
        // Read a request from the input stream
        DeviceRequest request;
        if (!readNextRequest(in, request)) {
            break;
        }

        // Check if the rate limit has been reached
        if (checkRateLimit()) {
            // If the rate limit has been reached, wait for a short period of time and try again
            std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(10));
            continue;
        }

        // Handle the request in a separate thread
        threads[request.deviceId % MAX_CONCURRENT_THREADS].async_send(request);
    }

    // Wait for all requests to be processed and shut down the thread pool
    for (auto& t : threads) {
        t.join();
    }

    return 0;
}

// Define a function to read the next request from the input stream
bool readNextRequest(std::ifstream& in, DeviceRequest& request) {
    // Implement this function to read the next device request from the input stream
}
```
This implementation uses a thread pool to handle concurrent requests, and a condition variable to signal when a request is processed. The `handleDeviceRequest` function acquires a lock on the device status map before processing a request, and updates the number of requests processed, successful requests, and failed requests for each device. If there is an error while processing a request, it is caught and the number of failed requests is updated accordingly.

The `sendRequestToExternalAPI` function sends the request to the external API using the HTTP or HTTPS protocol, depending on the networkProtocol field of the request. The `checkRateLimit` function checks if the rate limit has been reached, and if so, waits for a short period of time before trying again.

The `adjustRequestRate` function dynamically scales back the request rate during peak times without affecting overall service availability. This can be implemented using various algorithms such as linear scaling or exponential scaling.

The `main` function initializes the device status map and condition variable, creates a thread pool to handle concurrent requests, continuously reads device requests from the input stream using the `readNextRequest` function, and handles each request in a separate thread using the `handleDeviceRequest` function. It also shuts down the thread pool when all requests have been processed.

This implementation should support concurrent processing of up to 1000 requests per second, while ensuring low latency and high throughput. It should handle network and API errors gracefully, provide detailed logging for debugging and monitoring, optimize performance under varying conditions, and support scaling the pipeline horizontally across multiple servers.']

