This code implements a modular Java service that generates detailed reports for a list of Pokémon, integrating with an external API to fetch real-time data on their types, weaknesses, and evolution chains. The service utilizes efficient caching mechanisms to reduce API call frequency and ensure data consistency. It also supports concurrent execution of tasks without compromising system stability or performance, ensuring thread safety and efficient resource management.

To handle up to 1000 concurrent requests per minute, the service uses a message queue to decouple data retrieval from report generation, allowing for asynchronous processing and improved throughput. The message queue is implemented using a `LinkedBlockingQueue`, which provides FIFO ordering of requests and ensures that only one thread can access the queue at any given time.

The service architecture is designed to facilitate future scalability, including support for additional data sources and features like battle simulations or habitat analysis. It also includes unit tests to cover all critical paths and edge cases, ensuring high code coverage and reliability under stress.

Finally, the service is documented thoroughly, providing clear guidelines for future developers to understand and extend the functionality.']

