The `ExternalAuthService` class is responsible for handling interactions with external authentication services, such as RESTful APIs or relational databases. This class can be extended to support multiple types of external authentication services, and provides methods for retrieving user accounts based on ID.

The `CacheManager` class handles caching of user data, with configurable cache expiration policies and eviction strategies. It also includes methods for updating and deleting cached user data.

Overall, this implementation is designed to be flexible and scalable, with support for multiple external authentication services and caching mechanisms. It also includes robust error handling and logging capabilities, making it suitable for production use cases.']

