The `deleteUserSubscription` method first validates the input parameters and then checks if the user has a subscription of this type using the `hasUserSubscription` method. If the user does not have a subscription of this type, an exception is thrown. Otherwise, the subscription in the database is deleted using the `database.delete` method and the cache is updated with the deleted subscription.

The `getUserSubscription` method first validates the input parameters and then checks if the user has a subscription of this type in the cache using the `cache.containsKey` method. If the user does not have a subscription of this type in the cache, it is retrieved from the database using the `database.findByUserIdAndSubscriptionType` method and the cache is updated with the new subscription.

