The function first loads configuration parameters from the config service. It then sets up a pool of worker threads to process the data stream in parallel. Each worker thread takes the next data point from the front of the vector, processes it using the data processor, stores it in the storage manager, and checks for anomalies using the alert service. If an anomaly is detected, an alert is sent using the alert service. Finally, the processed data point is removed from the vector.

The function also includes some error handling and graceful degradation mechanisms to handle external API failures or rate limits, storage costs that vary based on data volume, and multi-cloud environment support.']

