Here is a sample code for the task scheduler:
```java
import java.util.*;
import java.io.*;
import java.net.URL;
import java.text.SimpleDateFormat;

public class TaskScheduler {
    private static final int MAX_CONCURRENT_TASKS = 100;
    private static final long JOB_EXECUTION_TIMEOUT = 60 * 1000; // 60 seconds
    private static final long HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL = 5 * 1000; // 5 seconds
    private static final int MAX_RETRY_COUNT = 3;
    private static final String JOB_LOG_FILE = "job-log.txt";
    private static final String API_ENDPOINT = "https://api.example.com/v1/task";

    private final List<Job> jobs = new ArrayList<>();
    private final Map<String, Job> jobIdMap = new HashMap<>();
    private final Map<String, Integer> jobStatusMap = new HashMap<>();
    private final Set<String> runningJobs = new HashSet<>();
    private final SimpleDateFormat dateFormat = new SimpleDateFormat("yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss");

    public void start() {
        // Start the scheduler thread to monitor jobs and manage concurrency
        Thread schedulerThread = new Thread(new Runnable() {
            @Override
            public void run() {
                while (true) {
                    try {
                        // Monitor running jobs and manage concurrency
                        for (String jobId : runningJobs) {
                            Job job = jobIdMap.get(jobId);
                            if (job == null || job.getStatus() != JobStatus.RUNNING) {
                                continue;
                            }

                            // Check for heartbeat timeout and update status accordingly
                            long heartbeatTimeout = System.currentTimeMillis() - JOB_EXECUTION_TIMEOUT;
                            if (job.getLastHeartbeat() < heartbeatTimeout) {
                                job.setStatus(JobStatus.FAILED);
                                log("Job " + jobId + " failed due to heartbeat timeout.");
                            }
                        }

                        // Retry failed jobs and schedule new ones if needed
                        for (String jobId : runningJobs) {
                            Job job = jobIdMap.get(jobId);
                            if (job == null || job.getStatus() != JobStatus.FAILED) {
                                continue;
                            }

                            // Retry failed job up to max retry count
                            int retryCount = jobStatusMap.get(jobId);
                            if (retryCount < MAX_RETRY_COUNT) {
                                job.setStatus(JobStatus.SCHEDULED);
                                log("Retrying job " + jobId + " (" + retryCount + " of " + MAX_RETRY_COUNT + ")");
                            } else {
                                job.setStatus(JobStatus.FAILED);
                                log("Job " + jobId + " failed after max retry count.");
                            }
                        }

                        // Schedule new jobs if needed
                        List<String> availableJobIds = getAvailableJobIds();
                        if (!availableJobIds.isEmpty()) {
                            String jobId = availableJobIds.get(0);
                            Job job = jobIdMap.get(jobId);

                            // Schedule new job and update status accordingly
                            URL url = new URL(API_ENDPOINT + "?jobId=" + jobId);
                            HttpURLConnection connection = (HttpURLConnection) url.openConnection();
                            try {
                                connection.setRequestMethod("POST");
                                connection.connect();
                                int responseCode = connection.getResponseCode();
                                if (responseCode == 201) {
                                    job.setStatus(JobStatus.SCHEDULED);
                                    log("Scheduled new job " + jobId);
                                } else {
                                    job.setStatus(JobStatus.FAILED);
                                    log("Failed to schedule new job " + jobId + ": response code " + responseCode);
                                }
                            } catch (IOException e) {
                                job.setStatus(JobStatus.FAILED);
                                log("Failed to schedule new job " + jobId + ": " + e.getMessage());
                            } finally {
                                connection.disconnect();
                            }
                        }

                        // Sleep for the specified interval before checking again
                        Thread.sleep(HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL);
                    } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                        log("Scheduler thread interrupted: " + e.getMessage());
                        break;
                    }
                }
            }
        });

        schedulerThread.start();
    }

    public void stop() {
        // Stop the scheduler thread and remove all jobs from running jobs list
        Thread schedulerThread = new Thread(new Runnable() {
            @Override
            public void run() {
                while (true) {
                    try {
                        // Remove all jobs from running jobs list and update status accordingly
                        for (String jobId : runningJobs) {
                            Job job = jobIdMap.get(jobId);
                            if (job == null || job.getStatus() != JobStatus.RUNNING) {
                                continue;
                            }

                            job.setStatus(JobStatus.CANCELLED);
                            log("Cancelled job " + jobId);
                        }

                        // Sleep for the specified interval before checking again
                        Thread.sleep(HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL);
                    } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                        log("Scheduler thread interrupted: " + e.getMessage());
                        break;
                    }
                }
            }
        });

        schedulerThread.start();
    }

    public void addJob(String jobId, JobStatus status) {
        // Add a new job to the running jobs list and update status accordingly
        if (jobId == null || jobId.isEmpty() || status == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid arguments: job ID or status cannot be null");
        }

        Job job = new Job(jobId, status);
        jobIdMap.put(jobId, job);
        runningJobs.add(jobId);
    }

    public void removeJob(String jobId) {
        // Remove a job from the running jobs list and update status accordingly
        if (jobId == null || jobId.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid arguments: job ID cannot be null");
        }

        Job job = jobIdMap.get(jobId);
        if (job != null && runningJobs.contains(jobId)) {
            job.setStatus(JobStatus.CANCELLED);
            log("Cancelled job " + jobId);
        }

        runningJobs.remove(jobId);
    }

    public void updateJobStatus(String jobId, JobStatus status) {
        // Update the status of a job in the running jobs list
        if (jobId == null || jobId.isEmpty() || status == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("Invalid arguments: job ID or status cannot be null");
        }

        Job job = jobIdMap.get(jobId);
        if (job != null && runningJobs.contains(jobId)) {
            job.setStatus(status);
        }
    }

    public List<String> getAvailableJobIds() {
        // Get a list of available job IDs
        List<String> availableJobIds = new ArrayList<>();

        for (Map.Entry<String, Job> entry : jobIdMap.entrySet()) {
            if (runningJobs.contains(entry.getKey())) {
                continue;
            } else if (entry.getValue().getStatus() == JobStatus.SCHEDULED) {
                availableJobIds.add(entry.getKey());
            }
        }

        return availableJobIds;
    }

    public List<String> getRunningJobIds() {
        // Get a list of running job IDs
        return new ArrayList<>(runningJobs);
    }

    public void log(String message) {
        // Log a message to the console
        System.out.println("[" + LocalDateTime.now() + "] " + message);
    }
}
```

In this example, we have defined a `JobManager` class that is responsible for managing job statuses and scheduling new jobs. The class has several methods for adding, removing, updating, and retrieving information about jobs, as well as logging messages to the console.

The `start()` method starts the scheduler thread and begins monitoring running jobs. The `stop()` method stops the scheduler thread and removes all jobs from the running jobs list. The `addJob()` method adds a new job to the running jobs list and updates its status accordingly. The `removeJob()` method removes a job from the running jobs list and updates its status accordingly. The `updateJobStatus()` method updates the status of a job in the running jobs list. The `getAvailableJobIds()` method retrieves a list of available job IDs, and the `getRunningJobIds()` method retrieves a list of running job IDs. Finally, the `log()` method logs a message to the console.

The `Job` class represents a single job with a unique ID, a status, and a timestamp for heartbeats. The `status` field is an enumeration that defines the possible states of a job, such as scheduled, running, failed, etc. The `heartbeat()` method updates the timestamp for heartbeats.

The `JobManager` class can be used to add, remove, update, and retrieve information about jobs, as well as log messages to the console. The scheduler thread is responsible for monitoring running jobs and making sure they are up-to-date in real-time.']

