#include <iostream>
#include <string>
#include <forward_list>

void insertAfterFirstOccurrence(std::forward_list<std::string>& list, const std::string& valueToInsert, const std::string& firstValue) {
    auto it = std::find(list.begin(), list.end(), firstValue);
    if (it != list.end()) {
        // Inserts the new element after the found element
        it = list.insert_after(it, valueToInsert);
    } else {
        // Inserts the new element at the end of the list if the first value is not found
        it = list.insert_after(list.end(), valueToInsert);
    }
}
```
Explanation:
This function takes a `std::forward_list<std::string>` and two `std::string` arguments. It finds the first occurrence of the first string argument in the forward list using `std::find`, and if it is found, it inserts the second string argument after that element. If the first string argument is not found, it inserts the second string argument at the end of the list.

The function uses the `insert_after` method of the forward list to insert the new element after the found element or at the end of the list. It returns nothing and modifies the original forward list in place.

