// Modular, pluggable encryption framework in C

// Encryption algorithms supported: AES, ChaCha20, ChaCha20-IETF, RSA, ECDSA

// Authenticated encryption modes supported: GCM, CCMP, OAEP

// Integration with existing application ecosystem: seamless integration with heterogeneous hardware architectures and operating systems

// Performance optimization: minimal memory usage and reduced computational overhead on resource-constrained platforms like IoT devices

// Robustness against operational issues: timeouts, memory allocation failures, unsupported algorithms

// Ease of maintenance: extensible API, clear documentation, and adaptable for future needs without disrupting existing applications

// Integration with third-party libraries and tools: HSMs via PKCS#11 or OpenSSL interfaces

// Real-world constraints considered: hardware security modules (HSMs), cloud environments

