Once the input parameters have been validated, the method determines which encryption algorithm to use based on the length of the key. If the key length is equal to the maximum size of the AES key (128 bits), then the AES algorithm is used. Otherwise, the Triple DES algorithm is used.

The `ProcessMessage` method then initializes the encryption algorithm and decrypts the message using the appropriate algorithm. The decrypted message is then returned as a JSON response if successful, or an error message is returned in JSON format if any errors occur during the decryption process.

To handle concurrent requests efficiently, the service uses asynchronous programming with Task Parallel Library (TPL). The `ProcessMessage` method is marked as async and returns a Task\<string\>, which allows the caller to await the completion of the method call. This enables the service to scale horizontally to handle increasing loads by adding more instances of the service.

