The tool ensures data consistency across distributed systems by utilizing a centralized database that stores metadata for all project directories. Each server in the system maintains its own local copy of the directory metadata, which is periodically synced with the central database to ensure consistency. The tool also employs caching strategies to balance speed and reliability, with fallbacks in case of cache misses or database unavailability.

To handle network failures, the tool provides informative error messages and recovery options, such as retrying failed operations or synchronizing with other servers in the system. The tool also ensures thread-safe and fault-tolerant operations, supporting concurrent updates and queries across distributed instances of the tool.

The tool is designed to be easily extensible for future features, such as integrating with CI/CD pipelines or adding more metadata fields. It optimizes for performance and minimizes resource usage, especially under heavy load, by implementing efficient algorithms and data structures.

