This C# library, named SecureContentProcessor, provides a modular and scalable solution for securely processing and storing user-generated content in a high-load enterprise web application. The library uses cryptographic hashes (initially MD5 but upgradable to SHA-256) of user inputs to ensure each hash is uniquely identifiable with metadata such as timestamps, user IDs, and IP addresses.

The library integrates with an external third-party logging service and database to minimize latency and efficiently manage resources. It also implements a distributed caching layer to optimize read performance and reduce database load. A flexible caching strategy is defined that supports varying cache expiration policies based on content type and user activity patterns, ensuring cache consistency across multiple instances.

The library addresses the challenge of cache invalidation in distributed environments and implements a strategy to minimize stale data propagation. It also designates a hybrid load-balancing solution that combines static and dynamic strategies for request size, user location, and current server load to minimize load imbalance. The load balancer is designed with custom load-balancing algorithms that adapt to dynamic traffic patterns and incorporate machine learning models to predict and mitigate potential abuse.

The library implements a fault-tolerance mechanism that automatically reroutes requests to healthy instances in case of failures, using health checks and automatic failover protocols. It also ensures system scalability and reliability by optimizing for both CPU and memory usage during large-scale processing, balancing reporting accuracy with system performance during peak times.

The library includes comprehensive metrics and monitoring to track system health, performance, and resource utilization, providing actionable insights for proactive maintenance. All assumptions, design choices, and trade-offs are documented to ensure a better understanding of the system's architecture and performance.']

