This implementation uses a `RealTimeDataProcessor` class to handle the real-time data processing. The class has three main components: `dataSources_`, `dataTransformers_`, and `dataCache_`.

* `dataSources_`: A map of all the active data sources, each represented by an instance of a `DataSource` class. Each `DataSource` object handles the fetching of real-time data from a specific streaming API.
* `dataTransformers_`: A map of all the active data transformers, each represented by an instance of a `DataTransformer` class. Each `DataTransformer` object handles the transformation of the raw data into a format suitable for caching.
* `dataCache_`: An instance of a `DataCache` class that handles the caching of the transformed data. The `DataCache` class stores the latest data in a map, with each key representing a unique identifier for the cached data.

The `RealTimeDataProcessor` class also has a few helper methods to start and stop the processing of real-time data, handle errors, and log status updates.']

