The code also defines a function `handleError()` that catches any exceptions thrown during the processing of sensor readings and logs them via email, SMS, or webhook. The use of RAII and smart pointers to manage dynamic resources effectively is demonstrated in this function.

This is just one example of how these concepts can be applied in a real-world scenario. There are many other ways to implement these concepts, and the specific implementation will depend on the requirements of your application.']

