The function also simulates network latency by introducing random delays between 1ms and 100ms for each entry. This simulates realistic communication latencies and helps maintain sub-second latency while processing a high volume of requests. The function also simulates packet loss with a probability of 5% per entry, which is handled by checking the RX information tag value after the delay. If there is packet loss, the thread sets the values to -1 to indicate partial processing and logs an error message.

