* ECC_P256 (Elliptic Curve Cryptography, using the NIST P-256 curve)
* ECC_X25519 (Elliptic Curve Cryptography, using the X25519 curve)

These custom implementations are used when the `Cipher` class is not able to perform a specific encryption/decryption operation. For example, if the `encrypt()` function is called with a symmetric cipher type and an asymmetric key, it will use the `RSA` implementation to perform the encryption/decryption.

