The library also includes robust error-handling mechanisms to handle transient and persistent failures, including retry logic, backoff strategies, circuit breakers, and fallback values for unreliable connections. It also includes detailed monitoring and alerting for critical issues, such as data loss and processing delays.

The library is architected to support horizontal scaling, distributing data processing tasks evenly across available resources to prevent bottlenecks and hotspots. It uses a `ThreadPoolExecutor` to manage the pool of worker threads and ensure efficient use of system resources.

In addition, the library includes a comprehensive configuration interface allowing users to specify data source types, API endpoints, authentication credentials, and processing parameters. The library also enables dynamic reconfiguration without disrupting ongoing data processing using a separate thread for reading and processing data from all data sources.

The library is optimized for high-performance data processing, minimizing latency and maximizing throughput by implementing efficient memory management, caching strategies, and parallel processing to handle thousands of concurrent data streams. It also regularly monitors and profiles performance to identify and address bottlenecks.

Finally, the library implements secure authentication and authorization mechanisms for all external system interactions, encrypting sensitive sensor data to protect against unauthorized access, and regularly audits and updates security protocols to adapt to evolving threats. It also monitors system resource usage and dynamically adjust processing strategies to optimize performance and resource utilization.

In summary, this library provides a robust and scalable framework for managing diverse array of sensor data streams, ensuring efficient data processing and robust error handling mechanisms under stress conditions.']

